    "title_en": "Iron Nuclei with Energy of 10^19 eV in Extragalactic Cosmic Rays Near Earth",
    "abstract_en": "The paper discusses the fraction of extragalactic cosmic iron nuclei with energies of 10^19 eV that reached Earth from distant sources without fragmentation in intergalactic space. It is shown that the fraction of particles with energies E = 10^19 eV is significant (about 10%), even if the redshifts of the sources reach 0.2, and not only for nearby sources.",
